Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:07:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Wait for the complete Bot overflow-refusal receipt

The retry marker is not the terminal receipt: refresh_receipt can observe a
pending admission, then its off-loop settlement commits before _maybe_retry
checks eligibility. The refusal write preserves the old pending projection;
the later terminal write supplies failed/context_overflow. The test broke on
refusal alone and indexed a reason not yet published.

Wait with tests.waiting.async_wait_until for refusal + failed + reason presence,
then retain exact open_user_tail, context_overflow and admission-count checks.
No production retry policy, budgets or receipt contract changes.

Detection: parameterize the original test over ordinary execution and a gated
real refresh/settlement/refusal-write schedule. The reader sees the actual
intermediate file before the writer may publish its terminal projection;
all owned refresh/watcher work is released and joined even on RED.

Proof (canonical run_tests.sh, Python 3.14.9, HERMES_TEST_FILE_RETRIES=0):
- incident head 84930ce773: old whole file 6 passed; old exact ID 1 passed
- identical incident/main writer and fixture bytes before fix
- controlled old wait on incident and main: KeyError 'reason'
- fixed incident/main whole file: 7 passed each; exact ID: 2 passed each
- wrong production refusal and wrong failure reason mutants: 2 failed each,
  at the retained exact assertions; source restored and final 7/2 green
- scripts/check --base origin/main: 21 checks green (without runtime override)

Recurrence: occurrence 67, run 44837707834 job 136638624934, PR #3844.
The original CI's exact thread schedule is not recoverable; controlled proof
establishes the concrete publication race without attributing CPU starvation.
Card: t_eeeeee0000000037
